A non-interface conversion: a bidirectional channel is assignable (hence
convertible) to a directional one. One chan struct{} producer feeds both a
send-only and a receive-only demand. The receive-only target renders as
(<-chan struct{})(x) because <-chan would otherwise be mis-parsed; the send-only
chan<- struct{}(x) needs no parentheses.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

//plumb:build
func NewSignal() chan struct{} { return make(chan struct{}) }

//plumb:build
var _ chan<- struct{} = (chan struct{})(nil)

//plumb:build
var _ <-chan struct{} = (chan struct{})(nil)

//plumb:build
func Use(send chan<- struct{}, recv <-chan struct{}) int { return 0 }
